                <pb facs="0627" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg507"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/1004: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sterling</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-08-03T22:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 3,
                                1922—10 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 4—9:40
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>67. Your telegram number 53, August 1, 3 p.m. The Peruvian Government is of the
                    opinion that the complementary act should be ratified and ratifications
                    exchanged in the same manner as the protocol itself, of which it is an integral
                    part according to its wording.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sterling</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
